L1189: Correla3on of testosterone concentra3on with immune cells and soluble immune mediators in blood. The testosterone
L1190: concentra3on measured in each sample collected during the study was assessed for correla3on with the indicated
L1191: immune variables measured in the corresponding sample using the two-tailed Spearman-ranked test. The calculated
L1192: Spearman coefficients r and the P-values were graphed as -log10 Spearman’s P values (x axis) against Spearman’s r
L1193: values (y-axis) for each data set: leukocyte popula3on counts (a), propor3ons of leukocyte subsets (b) and
L1194: concentra3ons of cytokines and chemokines (c). The dashed lines indicate the significance threshold (P = 0.05); the
L1195: correla3on of testosterone with the variables situated above this line were considered significant (nega3ve correla3on
L1196: when -1 < r < 0; posi3ve correla3on when 0 < r < +1).
